abstract: >
  Exports Published H.J. Andrews Experimental Forest and Long-Term
  Ecological Research (LTER) publications from a SQL Server publication
  database to BibTeX or RIS, for import into Zotero. Provides a
  command-line interface for each format (db2bibtex, db2ris) plus a
  tkinter GUI for the BibTeX workflow, tools to reconcile a database
  export against an existing Zotero library, and post-import Zotero API
  tools to repair truncated author lists and Newspaper/Magazine Articles
  misclassified as Journal Articles (a limitation of BibTeX's single
  @article entry type that RIS's distinct JOUR/MGZN/NEWS types avoid).
  Table and column names are configured via a user-supplied query file
  (query.sql), not hardcoded, so the tool can be adapted to other
  institutions' schemas. This material is based upon work supported by
  the H.J. Andrews Experimental Forest and Long Term Ecological Research
  (LTER) program under the NSF grant LTER8 DEB-2025755.
keywords:
  - BibTeX
  - RIS
  - Zotero
  - SQL Server
  - bibliography
  - LTER
  - data management
